GAL16V8
THORU13

EN   DISC RESET A3  A4   REQ  SELTO BSY  RW   GND
DSN  U15CE U12CE SELO ACKO HOLD GO  RDP  FDCSEL VCC

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; SCSI (SASI) interface, 1F/2F option (U11, U12, U13, U15 socketed).
;   $FFF00 (A4=0 A3=0)  data port, REQ/ACK handshake done by hardware
;   $FFF08 (A4=0 A3=1)  write: select (ID bit on the bus, SEL until BSY)
;                       read : status via U15 (b7=REQ b1=C/D b0=I/O, raw)
;   $FFF10 (A4=1)       WD1772 (FDCSEL, pin 19)
; Inputs, raw levels:
;   DISC  HIGH = $FFF00-$FFF3F selected (74LS139 + U10)
;   RESET LOW  = reset          DSN  LOW  = bus /DS (pin 11)
;   REQ, BSY   SCSI bus lines, LOW = asserted
;   SELTO HIGH = SEL asserted for more than ~0.3 ms (R2/C1, U11B): timeout
; Outputs:
;   U15CE, U12CE  active LOW chip enables
;   SELO, ACKO, HOLD  active HIGH, through 74LS05 open collector to
;                     SEL, ACK and ACK_HOLD (HOLD high = DTACK held off)
;   GO, RDP       internal state (pins 17, 18 are not connected on the PCB)
;   FDCSEL        HIGH = WD1772 selected. Drives U10 pin 3; R1 (1K) from
;                 DISC keeps the floppy working when U13 is not fitted.
; Handshake:
;   write: wait REQ -> ACK, keep the cycle (and data) until REQ goes away
;   read : wait REQ -> DTACK, ACK only after the CPU has latched the byte,
;          ACK released when REQ goes away
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/U15CE = DISC * /A4 * A3 * RW * /DSN

/U12CE = DISC * /A4 * /A3 * /DSN
       + DISC * /A4 * A3 * /RW * /DSN

SELO = DISC * /A4 * A3 * /RW * /DSN * BSY * /SELTO * RESET

GO.T = DISC * /A4 * /A3 * /DSN * /REQ * /ACKO * RESET
     + DISC * /A4 * /A3 * /DSN * GO * RESET
GO.E = VCC

RDP.T = DISC * /A4 * /A3 * /DSN * RW * GO * RESET
      + RDP * /REQ * RESET
RDP.E = VCC

ACKO.T = DISC * /A4 * /A3 * /DSN * /RW * GO * RESET
       + RDP * /DISC * RESET
       + RDP * A4 * RESET
       + RDP * A3 * RESET
       + RDP * DSN * RESET
       + ACKO * /REQ * RESET
ACKO.E = VCC

HOLD = DISC * /A4 * /A3 * /DSN * /GO
     + DISC * /A4 * /A3 * /DSN * /RW * GO * /REQ
     + DISC * /A4 * A3 * /RW * /DSN * BSY * /SELTO

FDCSEL = DISC * A4

DESCRIPTION
CST Thor 20 expansion board, U13: SCSI/SASI control and WD1772 select.
Reconstructed from the schematic and the Thor system ROM 5.22 (see
GAL_U4_U13.md). Not the original fuse map. Uses complex mode (feedback
on pins 15, 17, 18).
